@@ -708,7 +708,7 @@ Selected inputs retain their exact bytes and SHA-256 digests: the Brief, existin
 1. Validates an optional `--name`, then the Brief. An explicit Task Name is safe lowercase kebab-case, at most 24 characters, and cannot be a Task ID; it need not match the title. When omitted, Posse derives a short display name from the title or uses `task` when no safe ASCII name can be formed. Repeated names are allowed, but lookup by a repeated name or title returns `task_ambiguous`; `t<n>` is the stable selector. For Change Tasks, the title uses conventional-commit form `type[(scope)][!]: description` (for example, `feat(app): enable outcome-first runs`) and becomes the initial forge pull request title unchanged, without an id or slug prefix; a Lead may set a later title with `posse retitle` (section 14).
 2. Checks `max_workers` (`worker_limit`). A Worker slot is held by every `spawning`, `working`, `needs-decision`, `blocked` or `stalled` Task and by every Change Task in `done` or `merging`, because its Worker stays live and can return to `working` for CI fixes, merge-target syncs and Lead instructions. A slot is released only when the Task leaves those states (merged, torn down, failed or lost), so a follow-up never exceeds `max_workers` and queued refill never takes a slot a PR follow-up needs. The cost is that Change Tasks awaiting merge delay queued Tasks. Review Round Tasks skip this check and are never refused or queued for capacity, because the merges that release done Change Tasks depend on those rounds.
 3. Resolves the Profile.
